      "bodyEn": "An aviation or airport-management degree (bachelor's or master's) is classroom- and project-based. It suits students who want to work on the management, operations or business side of aviation rather than in the cockpit.\n\nThese programmes are accredited as higher-education degrees — in the UAE, for example, by the Commission for Academic Accreditation (CAA) under the Ministry of Higher Education and Scientific Research (with KHDA regulating private institutions in Dubai). Entry is usually based on school grades, English proficiency (such as IELTS or TOEFL) and sometimes an admission test.",
