      "headingEn": "How to choose",
      "bodyEn": "Ask yourself what you actually want to do. If you picture a career managing airports, airlines or aviation operations, the academic degree is the fit. If your goal is to fly, you need licensed flight training — and some students do a degree alongside or after pilot training to broaden their options.\n\nWhatever you choose, no programme or school can guarantee a job, an airline or a salary. Compare accreditation (for a degree) or civil-aviation-authority approval (for a flight school), and verify everything on the relevant official source before committing money or time."
