      "headingEn": "What an offer letter actually is",
      "bodyEn": "When an Australian or New Zealand university accepts your application, it sends a written offer (often called a Letter of Offer). The offer sets out the course, campus, start date, indicative fees and the terms you must accept to take up your place.\n\nOffers come in two main forms: conditional and unconditional. The difference is simply whether there are outstanding requirements you still have to satisfy before the place is fully confirmed."
