      "headingEn": "What a packaged offer is",
      "bodyEn": "A packaged offer bundles two or more stages of study into a single offer — for example an English course, a foundation or diploma, and a place in a degree — so you can see the full route to your target qualification in one letter.\n\nPackaging is common when an applicant does not yet meet direct entry requirements for a degree, or needs to build English or academic readiness first. Instead of separate, uncertain applications, the package maps out a connected pathway to the degree."
