      "headingEn": "First, read the offer and its deadline",
      "bodyEn": "When offers arrive, the most important first step is to read each Letter of Offer in full — including the course, campus, start date, indicative fees, the deposit required, and the date by which you must respond. The response deadline is firm, so diarise it immediately.\n\nIf you are weighing several offers, line them up side by side and compare on the criteria that matter to you (course fit, cost, location, outcomes). You generally can hold more than one offer while you decide, but each has its own acceptance deadline."
