      "headingEn": "How to accept an offer",
      "bodyEn": "Accepting an offer usually means signing and returning the acceptance section of your Letter of Offer, paying the required deposit or initial tuition, and completing any enrolment steps the university specifies.\n\nFor international students, accepting and paying is what leads the university to issue your Confirmation of Enrolment (CoE in Australia) or the documentation you need for the next stage. The CoE and student visa application are separate steps handled after you accept — this guide covers the post-offer step that comes before them.",
