      "headingEn": "From undergraduate to research",
      "bodyEn": "If you want a career in scientific research, your degree is just the first step. Australian and New Zealand universities offer a clear set of research pathways that build from undergraduate study toward a PhD, the highest research qualification.\n\nThe usual progression is: complete a bachelor's degree in your science field, build research skills through an honours year or a master's by research, and then enter a PhD. Each stage develops your ability to plan, conduct and communicate original research. The specific entry points and any alternatives are set by each university — confirm them on the official graduate research page.",
