      "bodyEn": "Veterinary science is a long, clinical, highly competitive degree. In Australia and New Zealand it is delivered at a small number of universities with accredited veterinary schools, and programmes combine pre-clinical science, animal health and disease, and extensive hands-on clinical training in teaching hospitals and on placements.\n\nEntry can be either undergraduate (a direct-entry bachelor degree taken after secondary school) or graduate-entry (a postgraduate veterinary degree after a relevant first degree), depending on the university. Because formats and entry routes differ between schools and between the two countries, always start from the official veterinary-school admissions page for each programme.",
