      "bodyEn": "In New Zealand the English level for most student visas is generally evidenced through your approved provider confirming you meet the programme's entry requirement, using the recognised tests and outcomes published via NZQA. So the binding number is usually your programme's published English requirement.\n\nBecause providers and programmes vary, two students entering different courses can need different scores. Always read your specific offer's English condition and confirm the recognised test and outcome on the official pages."
