      "answerEn": "Not always. Your first country usually needs a national long-stay visa and residence permit. For later EU countries, an EU mobility framework may let you study there on your existing permit through a notification procedure, but implementation varies. This is general information, not immigration advice — verify each step on each country's official government website."
