      "answerEn": "It is a small, selective, interdisciplinary bachelor's — a liberal-arts-and-sciences programme — where you combine humanities, social sciences and sciences and declare a major later, usually taught in English. The model is well established in the Netherlands and exists in parts of Germany and the Nordics."
