      "headingEn": "Where funded PhD vacancies are advertised",
      "bodyEn": "In much of Europe, funded PhDs are advertised as positions tied to a specific project, so the search is closer to a job hunt than a university application. The most useful official starting point is the EU's EURAXESS portal, which aggregates research jobs and funding across European countries.\n\nBeyond EURAXESS, watch individual universities' \"jobs/vacancies\" pages, doctoral-school and graduate-school calls, and the pages of specific research groups. National research-organisation and institute sites also post openings. Confirm each vacancy's details on the official page that hosts it.",
