      "headingEn": "Germany",
      "bodyEn": "In Germany you typically register your address first (the Anmeldung) and then attend an appointment at the local foreigners' authority (Ausländerbehörde) to obtain your electronic residence permit (the eAT card), which carries your biometric data. Appointments can be in high demand in large student cities, so request one early.\n\nThe exact documents, fees and timing are set locally and change. Confirm the current process with your city's Ausländerbehörde and the official German government sources.",
