      "bodyEn": "Quebec universities set tuition using a tiered system based on a student's status, rather than a single flat rate for everyone. The province subsidises tuition for its own residents, so different groups of students can pay different amounts to study in the same program.\n\nUnderstanding which tier you fall into is the single most useful thing for budgeting, because the gap between tiers can be large. The tier is determined by your residency and citizenship status, not by your academic merit."
