      "bodyEn": "Canada's immigration pathways for international graduates generally combine a federal layer (run by IRCC) with provincial options. After graduating, eligible students may apply for a Post-Graduation Work Permit (PGWP) to gain Canadian work experience, and may later pursue permanent residence through federal programs (such as Express Entry) or through province-specific streams.\n\nThe Atlantic and Prairie provinces each have their own dedicated routes. This guide explains how those routes are organized so you know where to look — it does not state eligibility thresholds, scores or timelines, all of which are set by IRCC and the provinces and change frequently. This is general information, not immigration advice; verify everything on the official sources.",
