      "headingEn": "Why the credential name matters",
      "bodyEn": "At a Canadian college, the word in the program title — \"certificate,\" \"diploma,\" \"advanced diploma\" or \"graduate certificate\" — is not branding. It signals the length of study, the level of the credential and the kind of student it is built for. Two programs in the same field (say, business or computer technology) can lead to very different credentials.",
