      "bodyEn": "A Bachelor of Science (BSc) in biology or the life sciences in Canada usually begins with broad foundations — cell and molecular biology, genetics, ecology, physiology, and supporting chemistry, physics, and mathematics. After the first year or two, students typically narrow into a stream or major.\n\nCommon specialisations include microbiology, genetics, biochemistry, molecular biology, ecology and evolution, marine or environmental biology, neuroscience, and physiology. The exact stream names, course lists, and credit requirements differ by university and change over time, so confirm the current curriculum on the official program page."
