      "bodyEn": "Admission to a life-sciences program usually expects a solid school record with science and mathematics subjects — biology and chemistry are commonly required or recommended. International applicants typically also submit proof of English proficiency through a test such as IELTS, TOEFL, the Duolingo English Test, or PTE Academic.\n\nThe accepted tests, minimum scores, and required school subjects are set by each university and can change year to year. Some universities admit directly into a named biology major, while others admit into a general first-year science cohort and let students declare a major later. Admission is never guaranteed — confirm the exact requirements on the official admissions page before applying."
