      "bodyEn": "Economics pairs well with several subjects, and many Canadian universities offer joint or combined majors. Frequent combinations include economics with mathematics (strong preparation for graduate economics), economics with finance or commerce, economics with political science (useful for policy), and economics with statistics or computer science.\n\nThese combinations broaden your skill set and can open different career and graduate directions. The available pairings and how the credits are split are defined by the faculty, so review the official program structure when planning."
