      "bodyEn": "Political science examines how power, government, institutions and public decisions work — from domestic politics and political theory to the study of countries and political systems. International relations (IR) focuses on how states and global actors interact: diplomacy, security, international organizations, trade and global issues. Public policy and public administration look at how decisions are designed, made and delivered.\n\nAt most Canadian universities these are studied through a Bachelor of Arts. Some schools offer a distinct IR or global-studies degree; at others, IR is a stream or specialization within political science. The available structures are set by each department and listed in the academic calendar.",
