      "headingEn": "Aviation pathways in Canada",
      "bodyEn": "Aviation training in Canada is regulated by Transport Canada under the Canadian Aviation Regulations (CARs). The main pathways for international students are pilot training (toward a commercial pilot licence and beyond), aircraft maintenance engineer (AME) training, and aviation or airport management programs.\n\nPilot training is delivered through Flight Training Units (FTUs) — flight schools approved and overseen by Transport Canada — sometimes independently and sometimes in partnership with a college that wraps the flying into a diploma or degree. AME and aviation-management programs are typically offered by colleges and institutes.",
