      "bodyEn": "Several large Canadian banks and financial institutions offer student GIC programs aimed at international students. Because features — opening amount, fees, instalment frequency, online setup and customer support in your language — differ between providers, compare a few official bank pages directly rather than relying on third-party summaries.\n\nA GIC is not a study-permit requirement in itself; it is one accepted way to show living-cost funds. Whether you need one, and how it fits your proof-of-funds plan, depends on current IRCC rules, which can change. This is general information, not immigration advice — verify the current proof-of-funds requirements on the Government of Canada (IRCC) website before deciding.",
