      "headingEn": "Activating and accessing your GIC after arrival",
      "bodyEn": "Once in Canada, you typically activate the account by visiting a branch (or completing the bank's online process) with your passport, study permit or port-of-entry letter, and the reference details the bank gave you when you deposited. After verification, the initial release is usually moved into a linked chequing/everyday account you can spend from with a debit card.\n\nKeep the email confirmations and reference number from your original deposit — you will need them to activate. If anything about timing or amounts is unclear, contact the bank's international-student support directly. Do this early, because you will want access to living money soon after you land.",
