      "bodyEn": "A student GIC is only one part of your money setup. Many students also bring some funds another way (international transfer to a new Canadian account, a card that works abroad) for upfront costs like first rent, a deposit, or a transit pass before the GIC instalments begin.\n\nThink of the GIC as a steady monthly stream and your other funds as the cushion for one-time, day-one expenses. Plan both together so you are not waiting on a single source. None of these amounts are guaranteed to cover your full costs — build a realistic budget for your specific city and program, and verify current cost expectations on official sources."
