      "headingEn": "What changed when the Student Direct Stream ended",
      "bodyEn": "The Student Direct Stream (SDS) was a faster study-permit processing route that had its own set of upfront requirements, which for many applicants included a qualifying language result. SDS has since been discontinued, so applicants now use the regular study-permit application process.\n\nBecause this is a recent change, do not rely on older guides, agent materials, or checklists that still describe SDS. The current requirements, accepted documents and any language evidence are set out by IRCC. This is general information, not immigration advice — confirm the current study-permit requirements on the official Government of Canada source before you prepare your application."
