      "headingEn": "Types of on-campus jobs to look for",
      "bodyEn": "On-campus roles come in many forms, and you do not need prior Canadian experience for most entry-level ones. Common options include work-study positions (jobs funded specifically to support students), library and front-desk roles, residence advisor or 'don' positions, café and bookstore jobs, campus-tour guiding, peer mentoring, and assistant roles in labs or research groups.\n\nEach type connects you to a different community. A residence role embeds you in student life; a research-assistant role connects you with faculty and graduate students in your field; a peer-mentor role links you to incoming students and the international office. Think about which network would help you most, not only the pay.",
