      "questionEn": "Is a Russell Group university always better than a non-Russell-Group one?",
      "answerEn": "No. The Russell Group is a self-selected association of research-intensive universities, not an official quality ranking. Many strong universities and courses sit outside it. Judge a specific course on its subject-level reputation, outcomes and accreditation rather than on the group badge."
