      "questionEn": "Why is a Scottish honours degree four years instead of three?",
      "answerEn": "It reflects a distinct Scottish academic tradition in which degrees start broad and specialise gradually. The extra year is built into the structure, with wider subject choice early on before the honours years. England, Wales and Northern Ireland more commonly use a three-year model."
