      "headingEn": "How to apply and where to research",
      "bodyEn": "Undergraduate applications to UK universities go through UCAS; applications to Irish universities go through the CAO. Both use a single application with course choices and (for UCAS) a personal statement. International students apply through the same systems, with extra steps for English-language evidence and, after an offer, the student visa.\n\nUse official course pages to confirm module content, entry subjects, accreditation and any placement options. The Royal Society of Biology accredits many bioscience degrees, which can signal a recognised standard and a clear route toward professional registration — check whether a course you like is accredited.",
