      "headingEn": "Map the cycle: when each test falls",
      "bodyEn": "Admissions tests are scattered across the application cycle, so plotting them on a calendar is essential. The UCAT is typically sat over the summer before your UCAS application. UAT-UK tests (the TMUA and ESAT) and the Oxford MAT generally fall in the autumn, close to the UCAS deadline. The LNAT is sat across an autumn-to-winter window. STEP comes much later — around June of your final school year — usually as part of a conditional offer. In Ireland, the HPAT is normally sat around February.\n\nBecause some tests come before you apply and others come after an offer, you may be preparing for one test while waiting on another. The exact dates change every cycle, so lay out every relevant date — registration opens, registration deadline, booking window, test day, results — for each test you need from its official source, and work backwards to schedule your study.",
