      "headingEn": "EU vs non-EU fee status in Ireland",
      "bodyEn": "In Ireland, the tuition fee you pay depends on whether you are classified as an EU or a non-EU (international) fee payer. As in the UK, this is decided by residence and immigration criteria rather than nationality alone, and is assessed against detailed rules by each higher-education institution.\n\nNon-EU students normally pay international tuition fees set by each institution and are not covered by the State's free-fees arrangements. EU students who meet the relevant residence and nationality conditions may be eligible for the Free Fees Initiative. Because the criteria are technical and change, confirm your status with the institution and on the official source.",
