      "bodyEn": "A first reader often writes a brief summary capturing the file's strengths, narrative, and any concerns. Applications are frequently organized by region, and readers commonly evaluate you in the context of your school and the opportunities available to you. Context can matter: readers may consider what was offered at your school, what you did with it, and any circumstances visible in your file. This is one reason \"context, not just raw numbers\" is central to holistic review. Specific practices vary by institution.",
