      "headingEn": "Pre-dental is a plan, not a major",
      "bodyEn": "\"Pre-dental\" is not a degree — it is a set of prerequisite courses and experiences you complete alongside any undergraduate major. Students major in biology, chemistry, or completely unrelated fields and still apply to dental school, as long as the required science prerequisites are done.\n\nThe core idea is to build a course-and-experience plan early: required sciences, the Dental Admission Test (DAT), relevant experiences, and a centralized application. This guide covers that structure only — it contains no clinical or treatment content, and following it does not guarantee admission to any program."
