      "questionEn": "Do I need a spike to get into a top US college?",
      "answerEn": "No. A spike can help an application stand out, but it is not a requirement. Many students are admitted to selective colleges with well-rounded profiles, and holistic review considers academics, essays, recommendations, and context together. There is no single formula. Focus on presenting authentic strengths clearly, and verify each school's stated priorities on its official admissions page."
