      "headingEn": "What CLEP is",
      "bodyEn": "CLEP (the College-Level Examination Program) is a College Board program of exams that let you earn college credit by demonstrating college-level knowledge in a subject — without taking the corresponding course. Each exam generally corresponds to an introductory college course.\n\nCLEP exams are taken on a computer at a test center, and most are multiple-choice. They are designed for students who already know the material, including self-taught learners, working adults, and military service members, as well as traditional students.",
