      "headingEn": "Who can request accommodations",
      "bodyEn": "Testing accommodations are available to students with documented disabilities — including learning, attention, physical, sensory, psychiatric, and chronic-health conditions — so they can access the test on a fair basis. Both the College Board (for the SAT) and ACT have formal processes to review requests against their eligibility criteria.\n\nEligibility is decided by the testing organisation based on your documentation and the specific accommodation requested, not automatically by having a diagnosis or a school plan. Many students who receive accommodations at school (for example under an IEP or 504 plan) also qualify on the SAT or ACT, but each organisation makes its own determination.",
