      "bodyEn": "Some analysts strengthen their profile with professional credentials. The CFA (Chartered Financial Analyst) programme, run by the CFA Institute, is widely associated with investment-analysis careers and is earned through a series of examinations and experience requirements. An MBA in finance, from a recognised institution, is another common route, especially for broader business and management roles.\n\nOther finance qualifications — such as accountancy or risk credentials — can also support an analyst career, depending on the specialisation. Each has its own structure, cost and requirements set by the awarding body.\n\nThese qualifications are options, not requirements, and none guarantees a job or a particular outcome. Compare them neutrally against your own goals, and verify each programme's current rules and fees on its official website before committing.",
