      "headingEn": "What fashion design study covers",
      "bodyEn": "Fashion design is a creative, technical field that blends art, materials, and the business of clothing. A formal fashion design programme — most commonly a four-year Bachelor of Design (B.Des) in Fashion Design — teaches design thinking, sketching and illustration, textile and fabric knowledge, garment construction, pattern making, and an understanding of trends and the apparel industry.\n\nThe goal is to help you turn an idea into a wearable, manufacturable product. Alongside studio work, most courses include history of fashion, computer-aided design (CAD), and an industry internship so you graduate with a portfolio and real workplace exposure.",
