      "headingEn": "Where a fashion design degree can lead",
      "bodyEn": "A fashion design qualification opens several directions across the apparel and lifestyle industry. Graduates work in areas such as garment and accessory design, fashion illustration, textile and surface design, styling, fashion merchandising and buying, and quality or production roles with apparel manufacturers and brands.\n\nSome graduates pursue entrepreneurship by launching their own label, while others move into adjacent fields like costume design, visual merchandising, or further study (an M.Des or specialised master's). Roles, demand, and pay vary widely by company, city, specialisation, and experience — research current openings and talk to working professionals rather than relying on any single estimate.",
