      "headingEn": "Core skills and tools to build",
      "bodyEn": "Employers usually look for a mix of technical and analytical skills rather than one specific qualification. The most commonly requested foundations are spreadsheet proficiency, SQL for querying databases, and at least one analysis or visualisation tool.\n\nStatistics fundamentals — averages, distributions, correlation, and basic probability — help you avoid misreading data. Many analysts also learn a programming language such as Python or R for larger datasets. Soft skills matter too: structuring a problem, asking the right questions, and communicating clearly are as important as the tools.",
