        headingEn: 'The curriculum: breadth requirements and the major',
        bodyEn:
          'Liberal arts colleges typically require students to fulfil distribution requirements — courses taken across different academic divisions (e.g. humanities, sciences, social sciences) — before or alongside completing a major. Some colleges use a core curriculum, where all students take a shared sequence of courses. Others use an open curriculum that gives students more freedom to design their own academic path.\n\nThis breadth is a feature for students who are genuinely intellectually curious across multiple fields. It can feel like a constraint for students who arrive with a highly specific vocational goal. Check each college\'s specific requirements on its official academic catalogue before applying.',
