      "id": "foreign-nationals-nri",
      "headingEn": "Foreign nationals & NRI applicants",
      "audience": "international",
      "bodyEn": "This guide describes the domestic counselling stage after a seat is allotted — acceptance fee, reporting and withdrawal — for Indian-national candidates.\n\nForeign nationals, PIO, OCI and defined NRI applicants usually secure Indian college seats through a separate route (for example the Direct Admission of Students Abroad scheme for many centrally funded institutes, or an institute's NRI/supernumerary quota) with its own acceptance, reporting and fee mechanics. Those processes are run outside the standard domestic rounds.\n\nIf you are an international or NRI applicant, confirm the reporting and payment steps on the official DASA portal or your institute's international-admissions page, and check any student-visa requirement for studying in India. Verify every detail on the official source before acting."
