      "headingEn": "Foreign nationals & NRI applicants",
      "audience": "international",
      "bodyEn": "This guide explains the domestic later-stage counselling rounds (spot, mop-up and stray-vacancy) for Indian-national candidates.\n\nForeign nationals, PIO, OCI and defined NRI applicants normally apply through a separate route — such as the Direct Admission of Students Abroad scheme for many centrally funded institutes, or an institute's NRI/supernumerary quota — which has its own rounds, deadlines and reporting. The domestic spot/mop-up rounds described here may not apply to you in the same way.\n\nIf you are an international or NRI applicant, confirm the correct process on the official DASA portal or your target institute's international-admissions page, and check any student-visa requirement for studying in India. Verify all specifics on the official source before acting."
