      "answerEn": "A counselling (government/convener) seat is allotted by the official authority purely on merit rank and your choices, usually at the state-approved fee. A management/institutional-quota seat is filled directly by the private institution for a defined, regulator-set block of seats, typically at a higher (but fee-authority-regulated) fee. Both lead to the same degree at the same college — verify the rules and fees officially."
