      "bodyEn": "Because TNEA ranks candidates on Class 12 marks, many applicants can share the same aggregate. To break ties fairly, TNEA assigns every registered candidate a unique random number generated by the system. This is a defining feature of TNEA that students often ask about.\n\nWhen two or more candidates have the same normalised marks, the tie is resolved using a defined order of criteria — typically subject-wise marks and other tie-breakers, with the random number used as a final differentiator. The consolidated rank list is then published on the portal. The precise tie-break sequence is set officially each year — check it on the official TNEA website."
