      "audience": "common",
      "bodyEn": "Seats are allotted round by round on the basis of merit rank, your locked choices, reservation and seat availability. After each round you log in to see whether a seat has been allotted.\n\nWhen you are allotted a seat you generally choose between two responses. Freeze means you accept the seat as final and exit further rounds — no upgrade, but certainty. Float means you accept the current seat as a guaranteed backup while remaining in the next round for a possible upgrade to a higher choice.\n\nFloat is the way to keep improving without losing what you already hold, since floating should not give you a worse seat than your current one. Read the official option descriptions each cycle, as the exact labels and consequences can be updated."
