      "audience": "international",
      "bodyEn": "JNU admits foreign nationals through a separate international-students channel, not the general CUET route. As a rule, foreign-national applicants apply either in-absentia (from their home country, without sitting the entrance test) or through recognised government channels such as the Indian Council for Cultural Relations (ICCR) for sponsored students, on supernumerary seats set aside for international candidates.\n\nBTech applicants who are foreign nationals are typically considered through the Direct Admission of Students Abroad (DASA) scheme based on JEE (Main), rather than the domestic JoSAA/CSAB counselling. Requirements, eligible programmes, quotas and deadlines differ from the Indian-student process and change each cycle.\n\nA valid Indian student visa is required to study in India. Confirm the current international-admission procedure, documents, English-proficiency norms and fees on JNU's official International Students page before applying, and check visa rules on the official Government of India sources. This is general information, not immigration advice — verify every detail on the official jnu.ac.in International Students page and the official visa website."
