      "headingEn": "The three main routes into JNU",
      "audience": "domestic",
      "bodyEn": "JNU is a central university, and since 2022 most of its programmes admit through national entrance tests rather than a single university-specific exam. Which test you take depends entirely on the programme level you are applying for.\n\nThere are three broad routes. Undergraduate and Certificate of Proficiency (COP) programmes admit through CUET-UG, the exception being the BTech programme, which uses JEE (Main). Postgraduate (PG) and Add-on Postgraduate (ADOP) programmes admit through CUET-PG. Research (PhD) admission uses national fellowship or eligibility tests such as UGC-NET / CSIR-NET / JRF, or GATE where applicable, followed by JNU's own selection stages.",
