      "id": "ug-cop-cuet",
      "headingEn": "Undergraduate & COP admission (CUET-UG)",
      "audience": "domestic",
      "bodyEn": "JNU's undergraduate offerings are focused rather than broad — they include BA (Hons) programmes in foreign languages and integrated science programmes, along with Certificate of Proficiency (COP) language courses. Eligibility (the qualifying exam, subjects and minimum marks) is set per programme, so read the specific programme's eligibility in the JNU e-Prospectus.\n\nThe process has two distinct steps that students often confuse. First, you register and appear for CUET-UG, conducted by the National Testing Agency, choosing the subject/language papers your target JNU programme requires. Second — and this is critical — you must submit a separate JNU application (with its own fee) on the JNU admission portal.\n\nSimply naming JNU as a preferred university inside the CUET portal does NOT create a JNU application. Candidates who only register for CUET but never apply on jnuee.jnu.ac.in are not considered for JNU admission. Verify the current programme list, required CUET papers and the JNU application window on jnuee.jnu.ac.in."
