      "questionEn": "Is an autonomous college better than an affiliated college?",
      "answerEn": "Not automatically. Autonomy means more academic control (own syllabus and exams), which can allow faster curriculum updates. But it does not by itself make a college \"better\" — you should still weigh accreditation, the specific programme, faculty, and fit. Judge a college on the full picture, not the label."
