      "questionEn": "Is a deemed university a real university?",
      "answerEn": "Yes — a genuine deemed-to-be-university is granted the academic status and privileges of a university under Section 3 of the UGC Act, 1956, and can award its own recognised degrees. The difference is how it was established (declared by the Central Government on UGC advice, rather than created by an Act). Always confirm the status on UGC's official list."
