      "questionEn": "What does 'Institution of Eminence' mean?",
      "answerEn": "It is an official status granted by the Ministry of Education and UGC to a small set of higher-education institutions, giving them greater autonomy (and, for public institutions, additional funding) to develop toward world-class standing. It is an enabling status, not a ranking or a guarantee of quality for every course."
