      "questionEn": "What is a statutory council in Indian education?",
      "answerEn": "A statutory council is a body set up under an Act of Parliament to regulate education and professional practice in a specific field — for example the NMC for medicine, BCI for law, PCI for pharmacy and COA for architecture. For many professions, your degree must come from a council-recognised programme to be valid for registration or practice."
