    {
      "questionEn": "What is the difference between an ABC ID and an APAAR ID?",
      "answerEn": "APAAR (Automated Permanent Academic Account Registry) is a unique student registry identity under the 'One Nation, One Student ID' initiative, accessed through DigiLocker, while the ABC ID is the identity used to hold and manage your credits in the Academic Bank of Credits. Per the official portal they are integrated parts of the same student-record ecosystem, so the APAAR-linked identity is what gives you access to ABC services. For exact definitions and current usage, refer to the official ABC and UGC pages."
    }
