      "headingEn": "This guide is about studying in India from Nepal only",
      "bodyEn": "India is one of the most chosen study destinations for students from Nepal, and the practical picture for a Nepali applicant is unlike that of almost any other foreign national. That difference comes from the specific, long-standing India-Nepal relationship and the open land border between the two countries — arrangements that do not apply to students coming from other countries.\n\nThis page is written for students from Nepal specifically. It explains how the entry side works for Nepali citizens, the ID and registration side, the admission routes Nepali students commonly use, and the official scholarship channels that include Nepal. It is general information only, not legal or immigration advice, and it deliberately does not state fees, quotas, cut-offs, or deadlines — those are set officially and change. Confirm your own situation on the official sources linked at the end before you travel or apply.",
