      "headingEn": "The India-Nepal open border and the no-student-visa position",
      "bodyEn": "The single most important point for a Nepali student is the open border. India and Nepal share a long, open land frontier that people from both countries cross without the visa formalities that apply to other nationalities. As a practical result, a Nepali citizen generally does not need a conventional student visa to study in India — which is a genuinely different starting point from students arriving from any other country, who typically must obtain an Indian student visa before enrolling.\n\nThis is stated as a neutral, practical fact, not as advice, and not as a comment on either government's policy. What documents you should carry when crossing, how your stay and study are recorded, and any conditions attached are all matters the Government of India determines and can update. Treat the open-border, no-student-visa position as a general orientation and verify the exact current requirements for a Nepali student with the Bureau of Immigration / Government of India and, where useful, the Embassy of India in Kathmandu.",
