      "bodyEn": "Because a Nepali student typically enters without a visa stamp in the usual sense, carrying acceptable identity documents is the practical part to get right. In everyday terms Nepali travellers commonly rely on a recognised national identity or travel document accepted at the open border; which documents are accepted, and whether any registration or reporting step applies to a longer study stay, are decided by the Indian authorities and depend on your circumstances.\n\nDo not rely on informal summaries for this. Check the current, official expectations for a Nepali national studying in India on the Bureau of Immigration source, and ask your Indian institution's international-students office — they handle Nepali admissions routinely and will tell you exactly what they need on file. This remains general information, not immigration advice.",
