      "bodyEn": "On the admission side, Nepali students are unusually flexible in how they can apply. Many sit the same Indian entrance examinations as domestic candidates and apply through the general route; others apply as foreign candidates through an institution's international-admissions channel where that is offered. Which path is open to you depends entirely on the individual institution's rules for the specific programme — some treat Nepali applicants under general/merit routes, others place them under a foreign-student category.\n\nBecause of this, do not assume one single route. For each programme you are considering, read that institution's own admissions page to see whether Nepali applicants apply as general candidates (often via the relevant entrance test) or as foreign nationals, and how it assesses the equivalence of your Nepali qualifications. The Government of India's Study in India portal is a useful starting point for participating institutions and their foreign-student processes.",
