      "questionEn": "Should I skip low-weightage chapters?",
      "answerEn": "No. Use weightage to prioritise and sequence your study — reinforcing heavier areas first — but not to skip parts of the syllabus. NEET spans the full syllabus, so leaving gaps is risky in a competitive exam. Study everything, and give extra time to both high-yield areas and your own weak topics.",
