    {
      "questionEn": "Is CPEng the same as Chartered Membership (CMEngNZ)?",
      "answerEn": "No. CPEng is a statutory registration and a legally protected title; Chartered Membership (CMEngNZ) is a professional membership grade of Engineering New Zealand. They are assessed against similar competence standards and are related, but they are not the same, and you do not need to be an Engineering New Zealand member to apply for CPEng. Confirm the current definitions on the official site.",
      "audience": "common"
    },
    {
      "questionEn": "Does CPEng let me work in New Zealand?",
      "answerEn": "No. CPEng is a professional registration confirming your engineering competence — it does not grant the right to live or work in New Zealand. Immigration is a separate decision made by Immigration New Zealand under its own rules. CPEng or a credential check may support an employer's or immigration pathway's evidence requirements, but it is not a visa. This is general information, not immigration advice — verify current rules at immigration.govt.nz.",
      "audience": "common"
    },
    {
      "questionEn": "Is CPEng assessed on my degree or my experience?",
      "answerEn": "Both. The Washington Accord-accredited degree (or demonstrated equivalent knowledge) is the education benchmark, but CPEng is fundamentally about demonstrated competence: a peer panel evaluates evidence from your own engineering work in a nominated practice area, with referees and usually an interview. There are no guaranteed outcomes — the assessment is evidence-based and individual.",
      "audience": "common"
    },
    {
      "questionEn": "How long does CPEng take?",
      "answerEn": "There is no single fixed timeframe. It depends on whether you need a knowledge assessment to reach the Washington Accord benchmark, how strong your competence evidence is, and scheduling of panel review. Prepare thorough documentation of your work early, and check current processing information for each step on the official Engineering New Zealand website.",
      "audience": "common"
    }
