      "questionEn": "How do I actually register to practise after graduating?",
      "answerEn": "In Australia you apply to the Optometry Board of Australia via AHPRA; in New Zealand you apply to the Optometrists and Dispensing Opticians Board (ODOB) and hold a current practising certificate. Graduating from an accredited program makes you eligible to apply — it does not register you automatically. No course guarantees registration."
