      "headingEn": "How to build a realistic family budget",
      "audience": "common",
      "bodyEn": "Put the pieces together in order: start with the official per-dependant funds benchmarks (from Home Affairs or Immigration New Zealand), add current family health-cover quotes, add school fees for each child based on the specific state/territory or New Zealand rules, then add realistic family living costs for your chosen city. Cross-check accommodation against real rental listings for a family-sized place.\n\nBecause every figure here is set by a government or provider and updated regularly, verify each one on the official source before you commit — and remember the standing rule that immigration and fee rules change, so confirm current requirements before acting. This guide gives you the categories to plan around; it cannot give you a guaranteed total, and it is general information, not immigration or financial advice."
