      "questionEn": "What is bulk billing and how does a gap fee work?",
      "answerEn": "In Australia, a bulk-billing clinic accepts the Medicare-scheduled fee as full payment, so you pay nothing at the visit. A non-bulk-billing clinic charges its own fee; your OSHC pays a benefit based on the MBS fee and you pay the difference, called the gap. Ask whether a clinic bulk bills or has a no-gap arrangement with your insurer before booking.",
      "audience": "common"
