      "headingEn": "Who SFU is",
      "bodyEn": "Simon Fraser University is a public research university in British Columbia, with campuses in Burnaby, Vancouver and Surrey. It is known for its co-operative education (co-op) programs and a broad range of degrees across arts, science, business, communication, computing, engineering and health.\n\nSFU has its own large intake and its own admission process — it is worth learning that process on its own terms rather than assuming it mirrors other BC universities. This guide covers the official route for international undergraduate applicants and defers all changeable numbers (grades, fees, deadlines, any ranking) to SFU's own pages.",
