      "questionEn": "Can the spouse of any international student in Canada get an open work permit?",
      "answerEn": "No. Since January 21, 2025, this open work permit is generally limited to partners of students in specific programs — typically a master's program of at least the minimum length IRCC sets, a doctoral program, or a select professional program. Partners of students in most bachelor's, diploma or certificate programs are usually not eligible. Confirm the current list on IRCC. This is general information, not immigration advice.",
